-- coa29-sch6.l4: Companies Act 2006 (United Kingdom), 2006 c. 46, SCHEDULE 6 "Meaning of "subsidiary" etc: supplementary provisions".
-- Layer 1 (the law, objectively). Generated by work/build.py from work/src/coa29-sch6.l4; quote lines are produced by srcrefs.py.
--
-- SOURCE. A plain-text rendering of the Act from legislation.gov.uk (Open Government Licence v3.0) made by a converter script; it is
-- not the official text and nothing here is "verified against the official text". Line numbers are of ukpga-2006-46.txt.
-- TARGET. The stable `l4` (main) 1.6.110. No section GIVEN, no REFUSE, no sets, no TYPICALLY, no YMD.
--
-- WHAT THIS SCHEDULE DOES. Section 1159 (the keel's, coa-definitions.l4) says a company is a subsidiary of another if the other "holds a
-- majority of the voting rights in it" (1)(a), "has the right to appoint or remove a majority of its board of directors" (1)(b) or controls
-- a majority of the voting rights by agreement (1)(c). This Schedule explains those expressions: which rights count, and whose they are
-- treated as being. Its answers are the facts the keel's `s 1159(1) link` takes (PLAN.md section 4.2): the lead wires them at the merge.
-- No function is imported from the keel; no rule of s 1159 is restated here.
--
-- READING A RESULT (rule of 2026-10-29, assumed, not ruled by a lawyer): JUST TRUE = the text says the case is within the provision;
-- JUST FALSE = the text says no in its own words (a "means"/"are to" definition, "unless", "only if", a flat negative, an unmet "where" or
-- "if"); NOTHING = the text does not decide (a rule limited by its own wording, "include", silent).
--
-- "THE OTHER COMPANY" is the company that may be the holding company; "the company" is the one that may be its subsidiary.

§ `Schedule 6 -- Meaning of "subsidiary" etc: supplementary provisions`

-- Who holds a block of rights in the company, seen from the other company (the possible holding company).
DECLARE `sch 6 who holds the rights` IS ONE OF
    `sch 6 the other company itself`
    `sch 6 a subsidiary company of the other company`
    `sch 6 someone else`

-- In what capacity they are held (paragraphs 5, 6 and 7).
DECLARE `sch 6 how the rights are held` IS ONE OF
    `sch 6 held beneficially`
    `sch 6 held in a fiduciary capacity`
    `sch 6 held as nominee for the other company`
    `sch 6 held as nominee for someone else`
    `sch 6 held by way of security provided by the other company`
    `sch 6 held by way of security provided by someone else`

§§ `Voting rights in a company (para 2)`

-- src:19558 | 2 In section 1159(1)(a) and (c) the references to the voting rights in a company are to the rights conferred on shareholders in respect of their shares or, in the case of a company not having a share capital, on members, to vote at general meetings of the company on all, or substantially all, matters.
@ref sch 6 para 2 Voting rights in a company (src:19558)
GIVEN `the company has a share capital` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the rights are conferred on shareholders in respect of their shares` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the rights are conferred on members` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the rights are to vote at general meetings of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the rights are to vote on all, or substantially all, matters` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 6 para 2 the rights are voting rights in the company` MEANS
    IF       `the rights are to vote at general meetings of the company`
         AND `the rights are to vote on all, or substantially all, matters`
         AND (   (`the company has a share capital` AND `the rights are conferred on shareholders in respect of their shares`)
              OR ((NOT (`the company has a share capital`)) AND `the rights are conferred on members`))
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the references to the voting rights in a company are to the rights conferred on shareholders in respect of their shares or, in the case of a company not having a share capital, on members, to vote at general meetings of the company on all, or substantially all, matters"

§§ `Right to appoint or remove a majority of the directors (para 3)`

-- src:19560 | 3 (1) In section 1159(1)(b) the reference to the right to appoint or remove a majority of the board of directors is to the right to appoint or remove directors holding a majority of the voting rights at meetings of the board on all, or substantially all, matters.
@ref sch 6 para 3(1) A majority of the board of directors (src:19560)
GIVEN `the votes at meetings of the board held by the directors the right is a right to appoint or remove` IS A NUMBER
      `all the votes at meetings of the board` IS A NUMBER
      `the votes at meetings of the board are on all, or substantially all, matters` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 6 para 3(1) the right is a right to appoint or remove a majority of the board of directors` MEANS
    IF       `the votes at meetings of the board are on all, or substantially all, matters`
         AND `all the votes at meetings of the board` GREATER THAN 0
         AND (`the votes at meetings of the board held by the directors the right is a right to appoint or remove` TIMES 2) GREATER THAN `all the votes at meetings of the board`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the reference to the right to appoint or remove a majority of the board of directors is to the right to appoint or remove directors holding a majority of the voting rights at meetings of the board on all, or substantially all, matters" (a majority read as more than half: fork)

-- src:19561 | (2) A company shall be treated as having the right to appoint to a directorship if—
-- src:19562 | (a) a person's appointment to it follows necessarily from his appointment as director of the company, or
-- src:19563 | (b) the directorship is held by the company itself.
@ref sch 6 para 3(2) Treated as having the right to appoint to a directorship (src:19561-19563)
GIVEN `a person's appointment to the directorship follows necessarily from his appointment as director of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the directorship is held by the company itself` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 6 para 3(2) the company is treated as having the right to appoint to the directorship` MEANS
    IF       `a person's appointment to the directorship follows necessarily from his appointment as director of the company`
         OR  `the directorship is held by the company itself`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A company shall be treated as having the right to appoint to a directorship if— (a) a person's appointment to it follows necessarily from his appointment as director of the company, or (b) the directorship is held by the company itself" (an unmet "if"; marginal reading (a))

-- src:19564 | (3) A right to appoint or remove which is exercisable only with the consent or concurrence of another person shall be left out of account unless no other person has a right to appoint or, as the case may be, remove in relation to that directorship.
@ref sch 6 para 3(3) A right exercisable only with consent or concurrence (src:19564)
GIVEN `the right is exercisable only with the consent or concurrence of another person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `no other person has a right to appoint or, as the case may be, remove in relation to that directorship` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 6 para 3(3) the right is taken into account` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the right is exercisable only with the consent or concurrence of another person`)
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A right to appoint or remove which is exercisable only with the consent or concurrence of another person shall be left out of account"
    ELSE IF `no other person has a right to appoint or, as the case may be, remove in relation to that directorship`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall be left out of account unless no other person has a right to appoint or, as the case may be, remove in relation to that directorship"

§§ `Rights exercisable only in certain circumstances or temporarily incapable of exercise (para 4)`

-- src:19566 | 4 (1) Rights which are exercisable only in certain circumstances shall be taken into account only—
-- src:19567 | (a) when the circumstances have arisen, and for so long as they continue to obtain, or
-- src:19568 | (b) when the circumstances are within the control of the person having the rights.
-- src:19569 | (2) Rights which are normally exercisable but are temporarily incapable of exercise shall continue to be taken into account.
@ref sch 6 para 4 Rights exercisable only in certain circumstances, or temporarily incapable of exercise (src:19566-19569)
GIVEN `the rights are exercisable only in certain circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the circumstances have arisen and continue to obtain` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the circumstances are within the control of the person having the rights` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the rights are normally exercisable but are temporarily incapable of exercise` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 6 para 4 the rights are taken into account` MEANS
    IF `the rights are exercisable only in certain circumstances`
    THEN IF       `the circumstances have arisen and continue to obtain`
              OR  `the circumstances are within the control of the person having the rights`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Rights which are exercisable only in certain circumstances shall be taken into account only— (a) when the circumstances have arisen, and for so long as they continue to obtain, or (b) when the circumstances are within the control of the person having the rights"
    ELSE IF `the rights are normally exercisable but are temporarily incapable of exercise`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): paragraph 4 speaks only of rights exercisable only in certain circumstances and of rights temporarily incapable of exercise

§§ `Rights held by one person on behalf of another (paras 5 and 6)`

-- src:19571 | 5 Rights held by a person in a fiduciary capacity shall be treated as not held by him.
@ref sch 6 para 5 Rights held in a fiduciary capacity (src:19571)
GIVEN `the rights are held in a fiduciary capacity` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 6 para 5 the rights are treated as not held by the person who holds them` MEANS
    IF `the rights are held in a fiduciary capacity`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Rights held by a person in a fiduciary capacity shall be treated as not held by him"

-- src:19573 | (2) Rights shall be regarded as held as nominee for another if they are exercisable only on his instructions or with his consent or concurrence.
@ref sch 6 para 6(2) Regarded as held as nominee for another (src:19573)
GIVEN `the rights are exercisable only on his instructions or with his consent or concurrence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 6 para 6(2) the rights are regarded as held as nominee for another` MEANS
    IF `the rights are exercisable only on his instructions or with his consent or concurrence`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Rights shall be regarded as held as nominee for another if they are exercisable only on his instructions or with his consent or concurrence" (an unmet "if"; marginal reading (a); a nominee in the ordinary sense is the input of sub-paragraph (1))

-- src:19572 | 6 (1) Rights held by a person as nominee for another shall be treated as held by the other.
@ref sch 6 para 6(1) Rights held as nominee for another (src:19572)
GIVEN `the rights are held by a person as nominee for another` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the rights are regarded as held as nominee for another under paragraph 6(2)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 6 para 6(1) the rights are treated as held by the other` MEANS
    IF       `the rights are held by a person as nominee for another`
         OR  `the rights are regarded as held as nominee for another under paragraph 6(2)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Rights held by a person as nominee for another shall be treated as held by the other"

§§ `Rights attached to shares held by way of security (para 7) and rights attributed to a holding company (para 8)`

-- src:19581 | (3) For the purposes of paragraph 7 rights shall be treated as being exercisable in accordance with the instructions or in the interests of a company if they are exercisable in accordance with the instructions of or, as the case may be, in the interests of—
-- src:19582 | (a) any subsidiary or holding company of that company, or
-- src:19583 | (b) any subsidiary of a holding company of that company.
@ref sch 6 para 8(3) Instructions or interests of a company in the same group (src:19581-19583)
GIVEN `the rights are exercisable in accordance with the instructions of, or in the interests of, any subsidiary or holding company of that company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the rights are exercisable in accordance with the instructions of, or in the interests of, any subsidiary of a holding company of that company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 6 para 8(3) the rights are treated as exercisable in accordance with the instructions or in the interests of the company` MEANS
    IF       `the rights are exercisable in accordance with the instructions of, or in the interests of, any subsidiary or holding company of that company`
         OR  `the rights are exercisable in accordance with the instructions of, or in the interests of, any subsidiary of a holding company of that company`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "rights shall be treated as being exercisable in accordance with the instructions or in the interests of a company if they are exercisable in accordance with the instructions of or, as the case may be, in the interests of— (a) any subsidiary or holding company of that company, or (b) any subsidiary of a holding company of that company" (an unmet "if"; marginal reading (a))

-- src:19575 | 7 Rights attached to shares held by way of security shall be treated as held by the person providing the security—
-- src:19576 | (a) where apart from the right to exercise them for the purpose of preserving the value of the security, or of realising it, the rights are exercisable only in accordance with his instructions, and
-- src:19577 | (b) where the shares are held in connection with the granting of loans as part of normal business activities and apart from the right to exercise them for the purpose of preserving the value of the security, or of realising it, the rights are exercisable only in his interests.
@ref sch 6 para 7 Rights attached to shares held by way of security (src:19575-19577)
GIVEN `the shares are held by way of security` IS A BOOLEAN
      `apart from the right to exercise them for the purpose of preserving the value of the security, or of realising it, the rights are exercisable only in accordance with the instructions of the person providing the security` IS A BOOLEAN
      `apart from that right, the rights are exercisable only in accordance with the instructions of a subsidiary or holding company of the person providing the security, or of a subsidiary of a holding company of that person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the shares are held in connection with the granting of loans as part of normal business activities` IS A BOOLEAN
      `apart from that right, the rights are exercisable only in the interests of the person providing the security` IS A BOOLEAN
      `apart from that right, the rights are exercisable only in the interests of a subsidiary or holding company of the person providing the security, or of a subsidiary of a holding company of that person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 6 para 7 the rights are treated as held by the person providing the security` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the shares are held by way of security`)
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Rights attached to shares held by way of security shall be treated as held by the person providing the security"
    ELSE IF       `the instructions limb`
              AND `the shares are held in connection with the granting of loans as part of normal business activities`
              AND `the interests limb`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall be treated as held by the person providing the security— (a) where apart from the right to exercise them for the purpose of preserving the value of the security, or of realising it, the rights are exercisable only in accordance with his instructions, and (b) where the shares are held in connection with the granting of loans as part of normal business activities and apart from the right to exercise them for the purpose of preserving the value of the security, or of realising it, the rights are exercisable only in his interests" ("and" read as requiring both (a) and (b): fork; a "where" condition not met: ruling of 2026-11-05 (b))
    WHERE
        `the instructions limb` MEANS
                `apart from the right to exercise them for the purpose of preserving the value of the security, or of realising it, the rights are exercisable only in accordance with the instructions of the person providing the security`
            OR  `sch 6 para 8(3) the rights are treated as exercisable in accordance with the instructions or in the interests of the company` `apart from that right, the rights are exercisable only in accordance with the instructions of a subsidiary or holding company of the person providing the security, or of a subsidiary of a holding company of that person` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
        `the interests limb` MEANS
                `apart from that right, the rights are exercisable only in the interests of the person providing the security`
            OR  `sch 6 para 8(3) the rights are treated as exercisable in accordance with the instructions or in the interests of the company` `apart from that right, the rights are exercisable only in the interests of a subsidiary or holding company of the person providing the security, or of a subsidiary of a holding company of that person` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE

-- src:19579 | 8 (1) Rights shall be treated as held by a holding company if they are held by any of its subsidiary companies.
@ref sch 6 para 8(1) Rights held by a subsidiary company (src:19579)
GIVEN `the rights are held by a subsidiary company of the holding company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 6 para 8(1) the rights are treated as held by the holding company` MEANS
    IF `the rights are held by a subsidiary company of the holding company`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Rights shall be treated as held by a holding company if they are held by any of its subsidiary companies" (an unmet "if"; marginal reading (a))

-- src:19580 | (2) Nothing in paragraph 6 or 7 shall be construed as requiring rights held by a holding company to be treated as held by any of its subsidiaries.
@ref sch 6 para 8(2) Paragraphs 6 and 7 do not reach a holding company's rights down to its subsidiaries (src:19580)
GIVEN `the rights are held by a holding company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person to whom paragraph 6 or 7 would attribute them is a subsidiary of that holding company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 6 para 8(2) paragraph 6 or 7 requires the rights held by the holding company to be treated as held by its subsidiary` MEANS
    IF       `the rights are held by a holding company`
         AND `the person to whom paragraph 6 or 7 would attribute them is a subsidiary of that holding company`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Nothing in paragraph 6 or 7 shall be construed as requiring rights held by a holding company to be treated as held by any of its subsidiaries"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "rights held by a holding company ... any of its subsidiaries"

§§ `Disregard of certain rights (para 9) and supplementary (para 10)`

-- src:19585 | 9 The voting rights in a company shall be reduced by any rights held by the company itself.
@ref sch 6 para 9 The voting rights are reduced by the rights held by the company itself (src:19585)
GIVEN `the voting rights in the company` IS A NUMBER
      `the rights held by the company itself` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`sch 6 para 9 the voting rights in the company after the reduction` MEANS
    IF `the rights held by the company itself` GREATER THAN `the voting rights in the company`
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the company cannot hold more of its own voting rights than there are
    ELSE JUST (`the voting rights in the company` MINUS `the rights held by the company itself`)

-- src:19587 | 10 References in any provision of paragraphs 5 to 9 to rights held by a person include rights falling to be treated as held by him by virtue of any other provision of those paragraphs but not rights which by virtue of any such provision are to be treated as not held by him.
@ref sch 6 para 10 References to rights held by a person (src:19587)
GIVEN `the rights are held by the person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the rights fall to be treated as held by him by virtue of another provision of paragraphs 5 to 9` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the rights are to be treated as not held by him by virtue of another provision of paragraphs 5 to 9` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 6 para 10 the rights are rights held by the person for the purposes of paragraphs 5 to 9` MEANS
    IF `the rights are to be treated as not held by him by virtue of another provision of paragraphs 5 to 9`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "but not rights which by virtue of any such provision are to be treated as not held by him"
    ELSE IF `the rights fall to be treated as held by him by virtue of another provision of paragraphs 5 to 9`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "References in any provision of paragraphs 5 to 9 to rights held by a person include rights falling to be treated as held by him by virtue of any other provision of those paragraphs" (an ordinary holding is not this paragraph's)

§§ `One block of rights, seen from the other company (paras 4 to 10 together)`

-- A composition for the seat layer. For ONE block of rights it says whether, after paragraphs 4 to 10, the block counts as held by the
-- other company. The inputs `the result of sch 6 para 4` and `the result of sch 6 para 7` are the answers of those paragraphs above.
-- The table (holder by capacity) is the Schedule's, one paragraph per cell, as the comments say; nothing else is added.
-- src:19566 | 4 (1) Rights which are exercisable only in certain circumstances shall be taken into account only—
-- src:19567 | (a) when the circumstances have arisen, and for so long as they continue to obtain, or
-- src:19568 | (b) when the circumstances are within the control of the person having the rights.
-- src:19569 | (2) Rights which are normally exercisable but are temporarily incapable of exercise shall continue to be taken into account.
-- src:19570 | Rights held by one person on behalf of another
-- src:19571 | 5 Rights held by a person in a fiduciary capacity shall be treated as not held by him.
-- src:19572 | 6 (1) Rights held by a person as nominee for another shall be treated as held by the other.
-- src:19573 | (2) Rights shall be regarded as held as nominee for another if they are exercisable only on his instructions or with his consent or concurrence.
-- src:19574 | Rights attached to shares held by way of security
-- src:19575 | 7 Rights attached to shares held by way of security shall be treated as held by the person providing the security—
-- src:19576 | (a) where apart from the right to exercise them for the purpose of preserving the value of the security, or of realising it, the rights are exercisable only in accordance with his instructions, and
-- src:19577 | (b) where the shares are held in connection with the granting of loans as part of normal business activities and apart from the right to exercise them for the purpose of preserving the value of the security, or of realising it, the rights are exercisable only in his interests.
-- src:19578 | Rights attributed to holding company
-- src:19579 | 8 (1) Rights shall be treated as held by a holding company if they are held by any of its subsidiary companies.
-- src:19580 | (2) Nothing in paragraph 6 or 7 shall be construed as requiring rights held by a holding company to be treated as held by any of its subsidiaries.
-- src:19581 | (3) For the purposes of paragraph 7 rights shall be treated as being exercisable in accordance with the instructions or in the interests of a company if they are exercisable in accordance with the instructions of or, as the case may be, in the interests of—
-- src:19582 | (a) any subsidiary or holding company of that company, or
-- src:19583 | (b) any subsidiary of a holding company of that company.
-- src:19584 | Disregard of certain rights
-- src:19585 | 9 The voting rights in a company shall be reduced by any rights held by the company itself.
-- src:19586 | Supplementary
-- src:19587 | 10 References in any provision of paragraphs 5 to 9 to rights held by a person include rights falling to be treated as held by him by virtue of any other provision of those paragraphs but not rights which by virtue of any such provision are to be treated as not held by him.
@ref sch 6 paras 4 to 10 The block of rights is treated as held by the other company (src:19566-19587)
GIVEN `who holds the rights` IS A `sch 6 who holds the rights`
      `how the rights are held` IS A `sch 6 how the rights are held`
      `the result of sch 6 para 4` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the result of sch 6 para 7` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 6 paras 4 to 10 the rights are treated as held by the other company` MEANS
    IF `the result of sch 6 para 4` EQUALS JUST FALSE
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Rights which are exercisable only in certain circumstances shall be taken into account only— (a) when the circumstances have arisen ... or (b) when the circumstances are within the control of the person having the rights"
    ELSE CONSIDER `how the rights are held`
         WHEN `sch 6 held beneficially` THEN
             CONSIDER `who holds the rights`
             WHEN `sch 6 the other company itself` THEN JUST TRUE -- the other company holds them itself (s 1159(1)(a)): this Schedule takes nothing away
             WHEN `sch 6 a subsidiary company of the other company` THEN JUST TRUE -- para 8(1)
             WHEN `sch 6 someone else` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): rights held beneficially by a third party are not attributed to the other company by this Schedule
         WHEN `sch 6 held in a fiduciary capacity` THEN
             CONSIDER `who holds the rights`
             WHEN `sch 6 the other company itself` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Rights held by a person in a fiduciary capacity shall be treated as not held by him" (para 5)
             WHEN `sch 6 a subsidiary company of the other company` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "treated as not held by him" (para 5), and not rights "treated as held by him" for para 8(1) (para 10)
             WHEN `sch 6 someone else` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): a third party's fiduciary holding is not attributed to the other company by this Schedule
         WHEN `sch 6 held as nominee for the other company` THEN JUST TRUE -- para 6(1): "treated as held by the other"
         WHEN `sch 6 held as nominee for someone else` THEN
             CONSIDER `who holds the rights`
             WHEN `sch 6 the other company itself` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Rights held by a person as nominee for another shall be treated as held by the other" (para 6(1): the other is someone else)
             WHEN `sch 6 a subsidiary company of the other company` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall be treated as held by the other" (para 6(1)), and para 10: not rights treated as not held by the subsidiary
             WHEN `sch 6 someone else` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): a third party's nominee holding is not attributed to the other company by this Schedule
         WHEN `sch 6 held by way of security provided by the other company` THEN
             CONSIDER `who holds the rights`
             WHEN `sch 6 the other company itself` THEN JUST TRUE -- the other company holds the shares and also provides the security
             WHEN `sch 6 a subsidiary company of the other company` THEN JUST TRUE -- para 7 (the provider) or para 8(1) (held by its subsidiary): either way the other company's
             WHEN `sch 6 someone else` THEN
                 CONSIDER `the result of sch 6 para 7`
                 WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE -- para 7: treated as held by the person providing the security
                 OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): para 7 attributes the rights to the provider only "where" its conditions (a) and (b) hold; otherwise they stay with the holder
         WHEN `sch 6 held by way of security provided by someone else` THEN
             CONSIDER `who holds the rights`
             WHEN `sch 6 someone else` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): a third party's security holding is not attributed to the other company by this Schedule
             OTHERWISE
                 CONSIDER `the result of sch 6 para 7`
                 WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Rights attached to shares held by way of security shall be treated as held by the person providing the security" (para 7: held by that provider, not by the other company or its subsidiary)
                 WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST TRUE -- para 7 does not apply, so the holder keeps the rights (the other company's own, or its subsidiary's by para 8(1))
                 WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether paragraph 7's conditions hold is not decided
